{
  "_doc": "The modular class system's terms: every thing is an expression over primitives (p) and other terms (t). One file for the Godot kernel (commons/modular/composite.gd builds it), the web tree (/knowledge-tree) and the tutorial path (tools/modular_path.py: derivation order = lesson order). Palle, 2026-10-23: 'point + mesh(color) + collider = sphere_collider \u2026 everything in this 3d world is triangles'. Primitives: point, mesh{shape,size,color}, collider{shape,size}, body{kind}, grabbable, label{text}, light. Operators: compose{parts}, associate{of,surface,story}, times{of,n,layout}, array{of,n,step,dims}, assemblage{parts[{of,at,rot,scale}]}, engine{of,kind}, transform{of,at,rot,scale}. A part with \"scaffold\": true is shown while the thing is being built and removed when it is done (Palle: the tape ends alone, line and points gone). A mesh may name a \"shader\" (ink: the drawn stroke, tapered ends, darker silhouette). {\"op\":\"sort\",\"of\":\u2026,\"by\":size|height|width|name} lays a thing's parts in a row by a reading of each (measure's first operator); {\"p\":\"prefab\",\"token\":name} stands a registry artifact in the grammar as itself. {\"op\":\"connect\",\"of\":\u2026,\"a\":i,\"b\":j,\"kind\":rope|rod|spring} (or \"ties\":[[i,j,kind]\u2026]) ties two parts of a thing by index \u2014 the strings.",
  "version": 1,
  "chapters": [
    "point",
    "line",
    "association",
    "triangle",
    "solid",
    "assemblage",
    "transformation",
    "array",
    "logic",
    "motion"
  ],
